{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/295304?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A295304"}, "id": "295304", "updated": "2023-03-07T02:24:19.525097+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "242", "page_end": "102", "year": 1990, "page_start": "97", "journal_title": "Phys.Lett.B"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Catani, S."}, {"full_name": "Ciafaloni, M."}, {"full_name": "Hautmann, F."}], "texkeys": ["Catani:1990xk"], "imprints": [{"date": "1990"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "We show that the large QCD corrections to heavy flavour production due to small \u03c7 logarithms can be evaluated and resummed in closed form, including the coefficient factor. The argument is based on a k \u22a5 -dependent factorization of the Born and structure function terms which is ascribed to Regge behaviour. The photoproduction case is investigated in detail. At high energies the total cross section turns out to be much larger than that obtained by a naive renormalization group approach."}], "control_number": 295304, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0370-2693(90)91601-7"}], "titles": [{"title": "GLUON CONTRIBUTIONS TO SMALL x HEAVY FLAVOR PRODUCTION"}], "author_count": 3, "document_type": ["article"]}, "created": "1990-04-17T00:00:00+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Lett.B%2C242%2C97&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value,document_type,impr